A few comments:

1) I had encounted a bunch of magic markers (3), so I happily wrote
several blessed scrolls of genocide.  I killed D's, H's, L's, M's, T's,
V's, & Z's, and I also zapped gremlins when I read an unidentified
scroll.  I think doing this really made things a lot easier.

2) I had real problems getting a number of common items (like boots of
speed, boots of levitation, a few rings, and scrolls of enchant armor
[argh]) but I picked up several rarer things, including many wands of
death, polymorph, and cancellation.

3) It's a lot of fun to polypile spellbooks.

4) It is just me, or are Archons incredibly tough?  I went through two
AoLS figuring out ways to survive an encounter with one.  I found that
wearing a blindfold kept them from 'stunning you with their blinding
radience.' Does anyone else know a good way of dealing with them?

5) A ring of conflict is essential.  I think it's one of the most
powerful tools in the game, and it probably should be toned down a
little.  Something to give you levitation is also really helpful. 
Levitation also seems to help when ascending from Hell with the Amulet. 
Being teleported down a few levels is *really* annoying.  A crystal ball
will save you a huge amount of time searching for those pesky magic
portals.

6) Reflection and/or sleep resistance is also essential.  I found the
portal to Fort Ludios, and when I was fighting the soldiers, they'd zap
wands of death and sleep at me like there was no tomorrow.  Without
reflection, I would've died immediately.  I think it's a major bug that
monsters can pick up and zap wands at you in one turn.  I would kill
someone with a wand of death, only to have something else wander in and
pick it up and start zapping it at me the next turn.

